---
title: Passeriformes
---
# Passeriformes

Passeriformes is the order of perching birds, holding more than half of all
living bird species. The defining character is the foot: three toes forward and
one strongly back, with a tendon arrangement that tightens the grip as the leg
bends, so a sleeping bird does not fall from its perch. Most members are small,
altricial and vocal, and the songbird suborder possesses a syrinx of
exceptional complexity. Families as different as [[corvidae]], [[ploceidae]],
[[turdidae]] and [[hirundinidae]] all sit within it.
